WEBVTT

00:00.000 --> 00:03.750
Silo. Computers for your agents.
Run Linux VMs locally or remotely.

00:03.750 --> 00:07.500
Start it here. Run it there.
Start, stop and monitor VMs across your computers.

00:07.500 --> 00:11.250
Connect over SSH.
Your editor and terminal. The VM’s files and processes.

00:11.250 --> 00:14.000
From server to browser.
Connect the VM's port 3000.

00:14.000 --> 00:16.875
A server in the VM. An address on your laptop.
Open your app at localhost:51432.

00:16.875 --> 00:19.125
Give agents a desktop.
The same your-app VM, with a Linux desktop.

00:19.125 --> 00:22.500
Read the screen. Click. Inspect the result.
Install your agent inside the VM.

00:22.500 --> 00:25.000
Choose what it can access.
Selected GitHub repositories. Read-only by default with OAuth.

00:25.000 --> 00:28.125
API credentials scoped to this VM and allowed HTTPS domains.
Stored on the hosting computer.

00:28.125 --> 00:30.000
Less setup. More building.

00:30.000 --> 00:33.750
Silo. Computers for your agents.
Download for macOS and Linux at silo.polarzero.xyz.
